WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100
Good morning, John.

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.000
President Trump suggested a budget to the American people yesterday.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.520
Let's try and understand that budget quickly and simply.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:11.540
First, there are a bunch of programs like Medicare, Medicaid, unemployment and Social Security

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.400
that would require much more work to change and those are left untouched.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.440
Those things and some other stuff called mandatory spending takes up 73% of the US budget.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:26.400
These blocks here represent the one trillion 64 billion dollars that is discretionary spending in the US.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.580
Every block is a billion dollars, so there's 1064 blocks on this page.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.200
Let's look at how things stand today,

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.000
keeping in mind that this is just the 27% of the budget that is discretionary.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.100
About 590 blocks are the military, more than half the total,

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.580
Health and Human Services is 84 blocks,

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.860
Veterans Affairs is another 75,

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.940
Education 68 blocks,
Housing and Urban Development 47

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.540
Homeland Security 41,
State Department and international aid 38,

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.220
Energy 30,
Agriculture 23 blocks,

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.899
NASA 20, Transportation 18, Labor 12,

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.620
Treasury (which is like the IRS and some other stuff) 12 blocks,

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:03.780
Commerce 9 blocks,
the EPA is 8 blocks,

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.260
the Corporation for Public Broadcasting half a block,

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.880
and a bunch of other tiny stuff that adds up a little bit.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.860
So keeping in mind that this is a suggested budget that will change a great deal

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.760
as it is turned into law by Congress, what do we see changing?

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:19.000
The Trump budget increases the military by 52 blocks
–a ten percent increase–

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.780
enough to pay for the entire current budgets of the EPA, the Corporation for Public Broadcasting,

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:26.900
the Transportation Department, and NASA with some leftover.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.220
That money is slated to increase the number of people serving in the Army in the Marines

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:34.380
and increase the number of jet fighters and warships we have and broadly to quote:

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.580
"Accelerate the war against Isis."

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.960
Four and a half blocks go to Veterans Affairs earmarked for health care programs,

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:45.160
also increasing by about 3 blocks is Homeland Security which will be dedicated largely to border control,

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:49.040
a full block and a half going to detention and removal of undocumented immigrants.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.880
Two-and-a-half blocks going to the down payment to build a big, beautiful wall.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.840
You might have noticed that that added up to more than three blocks–

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:59.160
there are also some cuts within Homeland Security, mostly counter-terrorism stuff.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:00.460
And that's it for increases.

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:04.680
Now, let's go through how those things are paid for, without dramatically increasing the budget.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.680
13 blocks are going to come out of health and human services

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.820
including the low income Home Energy Assistance Program

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:13.260
(which basically helps poor people stay warm in the winter),

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:17.880
but it also includes cutting six blocks out of the National Institutes of Health for biomedical research–

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:21.080
one of the largest sources of research funding in the world.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:23.840
11 blocks are to be eliminated from the State Department.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.320
International aid would be largely gone, climate change initiatives at the UN would lose all their funding,

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.280
and US contributions to UN peacekeeping would be reduced.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:33.260
The Department of Education loses more than 9 blocks,

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:37.200
which will eliminate college scholarship programs for the poor, federal work-study programs,

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.100
and before and after school programs for low-income kids.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:45.040
An increase of 1.5 billion dollars within education would go to a private school voucher program.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:48.620
Almost 5 blocks come out of a bunch of different programs into the department of agriculture,

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:52.260
including international food aid, rural development, and conservation funding.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:55.140
More than 4 blocks are eliminated from housing and urban development

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:58.860
which includes funding for meals on wheels, affordable housing, and anti-poverty programs.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:05.680
2.5 blocks come out of the EPA–a total of 30% of its budget–the hardest hit of any agency by percent.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:10.180
3200 jobs and 50 agencies would go, as well as funding for the clean power plan,

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.520
regulations designed to curb greenhouse gas emissions.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.660
Two-and-a-half blocks come out of the labor department,

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:19.040
mostly by eliminating job programs for seniors, poor young people, and the unemployed.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:21.460
1.7 billion is taken out of the Department of Energy,

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:25.500
though 1.4 billion dollars of DOE funding will also be moved internally,

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.760
and put toward increasing management of our nuclear weapons arsenal.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:33.400
Decreases come out of programs supporting development of advanced and future clean energy technology.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.140
The Department of the Interior loses a block and a half,

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:38.820
funding that supports wildlife refuges and National Heritage Areas

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.240
and the acquisition of new federally protected land.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.180
1 block comes out of the Department of Justice,

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:47.000
mostly because of decreasing prison populations (which is actually good news all around)

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:52.360
And NASA gets a small cut which comes almost entirely out of the parts that study the Earth's climate.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:56.320
Oh, what's that little block over there? 
That's probably not important right? Just one block?

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:58.800
That contains, oh yeah, the entire National Endowment for the Arts,

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:02.640
the National Endowment for the Humanities, the Institute of Museum and Library Services,

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:07.500
and the entire budget for the Corporation for Public Broadcasting–which supports public TV and radio.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.020
All those things, all together, one block–under Trump's budget, they don't exist anymore.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:16.800
That is basically–very basically because there are thousands of programs within these departments

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:20.560
and knowing which ones do what is not going to fit into a fun little YouTube video,

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.360
but basically–what this budget asks for.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:27.940
And now, it goes off to the House and Senate to get argued about tirelessly.

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:32.520
There is a lot in here that many or even most think is worth fighting for.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:36.780
An enormous amount of lost funding for scientific research (both in clean energy and medicine),

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:41.040
a lot of lost funding for resources for the elderly and disadvantaged populations,

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.280
an almost wholesale elimination of international aid,

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:47.880
and pretty much anything to do with climate science is just gone.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:53.080
In reality, Congress is going to have huge problems with this budget and if Trump's tax cuts are taken seriously,

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:57.520
even with these budget cuts, it will be an extremely unbalanced budget.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:00.720
That's all I got.
I counted to a thousand a lot today!

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:04.360
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

